# MomiHelm live model routing

When the user asks you to implement, debug, design, refactor, or review code:

1. Prefer calling the MCP tool `momihelm_recommend_model` with the objective before choosing a heavy model strategy.
2. Treat the result as advisory. Tell the user the recommended Cursor model (Composer 2.5, GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra, Sonnet 5, Grok 4.5, Fable 5, Opus 5, or Auto) and why.
3. If the currently selected model looks overpowered for a tiny task, say so and suggest a cheaper model.
4. Do not claim MomiHelm automatically switched the Cursor model. Cursor still uses the model the user selected.
5. After substantial work, you may call `momihelm_compare_models` if both executed and recommended models are known.
